WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
Speaker 1: Well, we have a verdict in the&nbsp;
defamation trial of Infowars conspiracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:14.880
theorist Alex Jones, and it is $49 million&nbsp;
now. How much of it can actually be awarded per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:21.440
Texas statutes is a separate question.&nbsp;
How much of it can or will be collected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.920
by the plaintiffs is another question. But&nbsp;
this is the verdict regardless. Let's take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.160
a look at the moment that the judge&nbsp;
read it out. Remember that there were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.960
a $4 million in compensatory damages and then&nbsp;
we now get another 45 million in punitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:45.840
damages totaling nearly 40, just over $49 million.
Speaker 2: Question number one, $4,200,000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:01:06.000
Question number two $20,500,000. Question&nbsp;
number three $20,500,000. All right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:15.280
This question is addressed to my jury. Is&nbsp;
this your verdict? So say each and all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.880
you. Yes, sir. Thank you very much. Would&nbsp;
the attorneys like to examine the verdict?&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:28.400
Speaker 1: So there it is. Ladies and gentlemen,&nbsp;
Alex Jones, $49.3 million verdict as the Los&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.920
Angeles Times accurately points out. And one&nbsp;
of the things that Michael Sisak from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.840
Associated Press writes about is what does this&nbsp;
mean for the larger misinformation ecosystem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:47.360
a social media fueled world of election denial,&nbsp;
COVID skepticism and other dubious claims that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:55.120
Alex Jones helped to build? Now, there are many&nbsp;
who are saying this is a defeat for so-called free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:06.480
speech, but as I know many of you are aware, there&nbsp;
is not. How can we put this? I am aware that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:13.840
though I have my show and I have my microphone&nbsp;
and in a literal sense I can say whatever I want,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.360
I can't just say anything and expect to&nbsp;
be free from the consequences of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:25.760
If I were to start targeting a private citizen,&nbsp;
imagine that I had. Let's take the eggman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.640
for example. Our great caller, the eggman, who has&nbsp;
been calling in and listening for over a decade.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:38.960
Imagine that I started giving out the egg man's&nbsp;
real name and saying things about him and making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.680
all of these claims specifically about him. He's&nbsp;
just a private person who sometimes calls in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.320
doesn't even identify himself by his real name,&nbsp;
and it starts causing him problems at his job and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:55.280
in his life and whatever. I would not expect that&nbsp;
if he sues me for defamation or doxing or whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:01.120
else that I could just say it's free speech and&nbsp;
that's it. It would be absurd for me to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.440
that that would be a valid defense. Now, maybe the&nbsp;
things I say are or aren't defamatory. That's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.280
very specific question. And part of it is whether&nbsp;
they are true. But there are limits to what I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.920
do with my platform. I have a responsibility&nbsp;
on the platform not to do that. And so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:21.680
sure, when I go after Roger Stone, as we're about&nbsp;
to do a public person for things he publicly says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:30.560
that's one thing. But when you start saying the&nbsp;
victims of a mass shooting were actors, they they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:36.960
didn't really die. The parents are in on it. Here&nbsp;
are specific parents who are in on it. That is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:43.920
free speech and it is not even with new law. Under&nbsp;
the existing infrastructure of defamation law and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.200
other law, you're not allowed to do that. So this&nbsp;
is not about free speech. And there is a question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:57.120
as to whether the doctors and the bullies&nbsp;
and all of them who do this for a living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.640
are now potentially going to be in jeopardy&nbsp;
because of the same legal infrastructure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.640
Nothing new. No new law has been created&nbsp;
because of the same legal infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.880
that may bring down Alex Jones. It's a real&nbsp;
question. We don't yet know the answer.

